1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,276
Welcome to Daily Brief.

2
00:00:02,226 --> 00:00:06,142
It's Wednesday, November 25th, 2026.

3
00:00:06,142 --> 00:00:08,809
Three stories in about three minutes.

4
00:00:08,809 --> 00:00:12,797
First, a shift in the mood around artificial intelligence.

5
00:00:12,797 --> 00:00:19,464
Anthropic, which only days ago completed the largest listing in history, has fallen below its issue price.

6
00:00:19,464 --> 00:00:30,059
According to industry reports, both OpenAI and Anthropic have also slowed some frontier model releases, telling partners they want stronger safety evidence before shipping.

7
00:00:30,059 --> 00:00:36,440
Put those two facts together and you get the phrase analysts are now using: a period of capital discipline.

8
00:00:36,440 --> 00:00:42,511
The money is still there, but investors have stopped paying for promises and started asking for proof.

9
00:00:42,511 --> 00:00:45,380
Second, a push for global rules.

10
00:00:45,380 --> 00:00:54,476
United Nations Secretary-General Antonio Guterres has called for a multilateral framework to manage the risks of artificial intelligence worldwide.

11
00:00:54,476 --> 00:00:59,642
He argued that no single country can govern a technology that crosses every border.

12
00:00:59,642 --> 00:01:04,833
The proposal has no binding force yet, and major powers have not signed on.

13
00:01:04,833 --> 00:01:10,535
But it lands at a moment when governments are struggling to keep up with systems that are already deployed.

14
00:01:10,535 --> 00:01:13,571
Third, the hardware boom is not slowing.

15
00:01:13,571 --> 00:01:21,976
Dell reported twenty two billion dollars in AI-optimised server revenue for the quarter, well above the nineteen billion analysts expected.

16
00:01:21,976 --> 00:01:30,833
That is a reminder of something easy to forget during a valuation debate: somebody is still buying enormous quantities of machines, and the money is real.

17
00:01:30,833 --> 00:01:33,571
So we have a split picture this week.

18
00:01:33,571 --> 00:01:36,380
Capital is cautious about the companies.

19
00:01:36,380 --> 00:01:39,404
It is not cautious about the infrastructure.

20
00:01:39,404 --> 00:01:41,630
That's your briefing for today.

21
00:01:41,630 --> 00:01:44,488
The full transcript is in the show notes.

22
00:01:44,488 --> 00:01:46,702
I'll be back tomorrow morning.

